      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The term \"brainwave entrainment\" might be an exaggeration, but the concept is being explored in various fields, including architecture and acoustics. There is limited specific research on high-end smart buildings using infrasound for \"occupant management\" or psychological manipulation. However, studies on infrasound and acoustic psychology suggest that human perception can be influenced by patterns of sound and vibrations, even below the threshold of human hearing. Technical specs and studies on \"acoustics of comfort and thermal acoustic comfort\" in high-end buildings may provide some insights into the design of these systems, although these studies are more focused on thermal comfort and noise abatement rather than manipulating occupant behavior.",
